From 7a57bda23fe58c777527d87fa47be269591c8580 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luis Atala <luis.atala@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:12:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] HID: razer-barracuda: add driver for the Razer Barracuda
 X (2022) dongle

The Razer Barracuda X (2022) is a wireless headset whose 2.4 GHz USB
dongle (1532:0552) is a composite UAC1 audio and HID device. Over HID
report 1 the dongle tunnels vendor messages from the headset: wireless
link changes, battery percentage and charging cable state. Razer does not
document the protocol; it was derived from USB captures of the vendor's
Windows software and from the dongle firmware.

Add a driver for the dongle's HID interface that:

- asks for the link state (E3) on probe and resume, up to three times,
  because the dongle sends nothing while the link is unchanged;
- registers a device-scoped battery only while the headset is linked, so
  that userspace stops listing the headset while it is off, as
  hid-corsair-void does;
- sets the USB wireless_status attribute of the interface;
- reports the link as SW_HEADPHONE_INSERT and SW_MICROPHONE_INSERT on a
  "Headset Jack" input device, as hid-playstation does, for a sound
  driver to turn into jack controls.

Frames are reassembled from report chunks and validated before use.
Acknowledgments, other command replies and malformed frames are never
link evidence. An unknown link, before the first reply and after resume,
neither registers nor removes the battery. Reports are passed on to
hidraw and to the generic input path, which handles the headset's
play/pause button.

The percentage is the last one the headset reported. The headset never
reports charge termination, so the status is charging while the cable is
plugged in below 100% and full at 100%. CAPACITY_LEVEL is always
UNKNOWN: without a readable level UPower does not list the battery until
the first percentage arrives, which may take minutes.

Add KUnit tests for the stream decoder and the state handling.

Assisted-by: LLM sparse
